    "turn_idx": 75,
    "turn_text": "Much more chaotic. There's no, there's no deadlines to do anything. And what I mean by that is, hold on my nose, this one. And what I mean by that is, is that in Tallahassee, session ends. It is a defined end to it every single year. The members know we have a balanced budget amendment, so we have to pass a balanced budget. We have to go through that process. We don't have a choice. It's in our Constitution. DC, no balanced budget amendment in our constitution, so they can kind of do whatever. Because we meet full time, we meet year",
