    "turn_text": "really no pressure to do anything or get anything done. And I think the other part is, and this is why I'm even more a supporter of congressional term limits now than I was before, but because there's no term limits, members realize that they can just stay as long as they want to. And so there's really no impotence to be focused on the things that are important to your district or things that are important to the country. You kind of just take your time as long as you want.",
