    "turn_idx": 93,
    "turn_text": "You are responsible. Like the member of Congress is responsible to keep your office under that annual budget. If you go over that number, you, the member of Congress, are personally liable to write a check to the United States Treasury for what you overspend. And that goes for everything. Staff, equipment, they call it franking mail, which is mail back to the district about different things that are going on in Washington. All that stuff is covered under the budget.",
