  {
    "episode_id": 46776,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46776.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 220,
    "turn_text": "anything. But you don't know what all this, I've been through college. There was a top part of my student loan debt was really just for me to hang out. And I'm going to be 100% about it. I'm going to be very clear. There were years in my college life where I was hanging out. And I was not serious, but I'm still having to pay that portion of the debt back too. It could have won a very different way. And I would have still had to pay that debt. So was it wrong for me to have to have that debt when there were decisions I made in my life when I was in college? And I think that's how we have to look at that and really understand it. The second part is, and we're starting to reverse it in Florida and the country. Telling people, young people, they have to go to college to be successful is a mistake. It is wrong. And we have misled a generation",
