    "turn_idx": 272,
    "turn_text": "Let's be very clear. The reason why they want they think it's important now and at a market of Massachusetts, just said it the other day, he said, well, Trump stole two seats. No, he didn't. He was, hey, how you doing? No, he didn't. He literally appointed people under the Constitution that he was legally allowed to do, but that's the way they feel about it. The big thing is the Democrats have been accustomed to the Supreme Court being their ideological bent for 40 years in the United States, and they want it back. And so they say the quickest way is packing the court. I think that you have Democrats who are going to have heartburn about this, and they're not going to want to support it. It should not happen, but we're going to have to stay vigilant on it.",
