    "turn_text": "their projects. I'll tell you right now that members on both sides of the island, Florida are committed to doing that. And so we're going to be pushing very hard and this infrastructure bill or other funding that comes forward to making sure that award money for Everglades restoration is in that budget so we can continue the work. It is critical that we get a couple things online. The C43 Reservoir should come online next year. That's going to help a lot. The biggest question is how do we get over this year? Lake level is high. There's algae forming in a lake. We're aware of that right now. My office and other congressmen's offices are in or we are on with Army Corps about the new low sum schedule of water releases. We're actually going through a couple of scenarios right now that I'm going to be sharing with my colleagues that we're going to take to the Army Corps for them to make those necessary adjustments in it. I was in the Everglades. I was in Western Everglades two weeks ago. on a tour and we have water level issues in the Everlades itself. And part of it is the core didn't release enough water there. And so what we have to get to is a more comprehensive schedule with the core in the short term. But intermediate long term is we have to finish the projects. It's just as simple. And then once we finish the projects, then we can have the necessary conversation about what are the other things that contribute to water issues we have. But I think finishing the projects is actually going to help a lot more people realize. The other good thing that's happening And we don't talk about much in our area are the water projects north of Lake Okeechobee,",
